    "body": "This isn't really a specification issue because exactly how permissions are managed is usually implementation-defined.\r\n\r\nIn Chromium, permissions to access a serial port are not always persistent. On Windows they are. On other platforms it requires the USB device to have a serial number. We've been tracking a feature request to improve this, but changes here have a security impact because they are only a heuristic.\r\n\r\nTo guarantee the ability to automatically connect to a serial port, you can use an enterprise policy such as [SerialAllowUsbDevicesForUrls](https://chromeenterprise.google/policies/#SerialAllowUsbDevicesForUrls) or [SerialAllowAllPortsForUrls](https://chromeenterprise.google/policies/#SerialAllowAllPortsForUrls) to control permissions instead of relying on the user-driven permission UI.",
